# Demo YouTube video

When a demo has a published walkthrough on YouTube, surface it on the GitHub Pages **detail page** — not on marketplace cards.

## Data

Add **`youtube_url`** to the demo’s entry in [`_data/demos.yml`](_data/demos.yml):

```yaml
youtube_url: https://youtu.be/VIDEO_ID
```

Accepted forms: `youtu.be/…`, `youtube.com/watch?v=…`, or `youtube.com/embed/…`. Store the canonical share URL from YouTube; the site derives the embed ID in [`_includes/demo-youtube.html`](_includes/demo-youtube.html).

Omit `youtube_url` when no video exists. Do not add placeholder URLs.

## Page behavior (automatic)

When `youtube_url` is set:

1. **`Demo video`** section renders **immediately after Playbooks** (before Demo ideas / planned artifacts). Wired in [`_layouts/demo-detail.html`](_layouts/demo-detail.html) via [`_includes/demo-youtube.html`](_includes/demo-youtube.html).
2. Section **`id="demo-video"`** — anchor for the sidebar TOC link **Demo video** in [`_includes/demo-sidebar-toc.html`](_includes/demo-sidebar-toc.html).
3. A red pill **Subscribe to our YouTube channel** links to [The Ansible Playbook on YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/ansibleautomation) (same on every demo that has a video).

Do not duplicate embed markup on individual demo pages or in `demo_pages.yml`.

## Checklist for new or updated demos

1. Confirm a walkthrough URL exists and is public.
2. Set `youtube_url` on the matching slug in `_data/demos.yml`.
3. Build or preview the detail page — verify embed loads, TOC includes **Demo video** after **Playbooks**, and subscribe pill styling matches the site.
4. Do not change `_includes/demo-youtube.html` or layout unless the product pattern changes for all demos.

See also: [CLAUDE.md](../../CLAUDE.md), [demo-site-copy.mdc](demo-site-copy.mdc).
